Actually, sql.js supports standard SQLite. Migration approach: recreate the presencas table with `lido_em TEXT` nullable, copying data. But careful with foreign keys. In SQLite, to change a column's NOT NULL constraint, you need to recreate the table (there's no ALTER COLUMN). SQLite ALTER TABLE DROP COLUMN is available in newer versions but only drops columns, doesn't change NOT NULL.

Recreation:
```sql
PRAGMA foreign_keys = OFF;
BEGIN;
CREATE TABLE presencas_novo (... lido_em TEXT ...);
INSERT INTO presencas_novo SELECT ... FROM presencas;
DROP TABLE presencas;
ALTER TABLE presencas_novo RENAME TO presencas;
